1
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:17,200
He targeted the industry. His own writing explains why. Now its workers are getting threats.

2
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:30,600
These were sent after his arrest. Did he send any of them? Use his words. They're here.

3
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,710
The writing is ours too. We're not relying only on the emails.

4
00:00:40,010 --> 00:00:44,710
Then address the charge. A public audience doesn't settle the intent question.

5
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,300
He meant to reach the public.

6
00:00:55,600 --> 00:01:00,300
You still have to prove the intent this charge requires.

7
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:17,800
The terrorism-related counts are dismissed on this record. This ruling does not dismiss the ordinary murder charge or determine the defendant's guilt.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,300
Can I take this?

9
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:23,900
Both pages.

10
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,200
All verified. The login, page access, doctor's signature. Send the redacted copies.

11
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:43,300
'Fully reviewed'?

12
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,900
No. We can prove that sentence wrong.

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,960
So the investigation was false?

14
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:58,180
That sentence was false. Quote it. Attach what proves it.

15
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,200
Send her the records. Tell her we want a correction.

16
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:17,800
Real?

17
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:21,400
Yeah. The signatures and the login sessions.

18
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,750
The receipts still don't match the denials.

19
00:02:32,050 --> 00:02:35,970
Then that's another question. This says someone opened the page.

20
00:02:36,270 --> 00:02:38,620
It doesn't say what they read.

21
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:42,060
No. It doesn't make your sentence true either.

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:57,300
You've got until six. Then the follow-up stays down.

23
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,900
Let me call her.
